Subject: [PATCH 07198/11362] [outer-loop] REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-17: tier-1
 max_nodes_reached wall recurs identically on cd82 and g50t

Repeated the REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-15/16 diagnostic (default max_nodes=20000,
budget=250, no code changes needed) on cd82 and g50t -- both drawn from this
REQ chain's original 4-game sample, both HIDDEN_STATE_GAME_IDS members, a
structurally different second-tier gate path than sp80's.

Result: the pattern recurs identically on all 4 new arm-measurements.
explored_out=False, is_level_complete_was_none=False,
termination_reason=max_nodes_reached at nodes_expanded 20005-20034,
planned=False for every arm (cd82: 20014/20012; g50t: 20005/20034).
Combined with sp80's prior 4 measurements, that's 6/6 arm-measurements
across 3 games landing on the same tier-1 exhaustion signature -- confirming
the wall is systemic, not sp80-specific, including on a structurally
different hidden-state-gated code path. Which second-tier gate fires
afterward remains game-class-dependent; only tier 1's exhaustion is uniform.

Scope limit: n=3 games out of the 25-game registry, all from the same prior
sample -- "likely dominant across the corpus" is now reasonable, "confirmed
for all 25 games" is not, per Sample-Size Rigor discipline.

